.mutate-inflight.json

# Generated eval cases: absolute paths, one machine, never committed.
plugin/evals/generated/

# Eval HTML reports: presentation only, regenerable from the aggregate JSON
# beside them, and 660K of a plugin every user downloads. The JSON stays: it is
# the evidence behind the measurements recorded in docs/BACKLOG.md.
plugin/evals/results/**/report.html

# Eval results are a local measurement artefact. `marketplace.json` says
# `"source": "."`, so anything tracked here ships to every user — 603K of
# aggregate JSON, 29% of the whole download, that nobody runs. They also carried
# the author's home path into a public repo for two days. The numbers that
# matter are written into docs/BACKLOG.md in prose, where they are actually read.
plugin/evals/results/
# AND the repo-root path, because `claude plugin eval .` writes ./evals/results/
# regardless of where the plugin lives. ADR-008 moved the plugin under plugin/
# and this rule moved with it, leaving the path the TOOL actually writes to
# unignored — CLAUDE.md §1's own warning, which is that a .gitignore rule that
# stops matching does not warn. Found 2026-09-02 by running an eval and seeing
# `?? evals/` in git status, one `git add -A` away from committing transcripts.
evals/results/
evals/generated/

# Any Python import of a gate writes this unless it sets dont_write_bytecode,
# and a dotless DIRECTORY in bin/ used to read as a gate.
__pycache__/

# macOS writes this into any directory Finder touches.
.DS_Store
.unasserted-inflight.json

# ADR-023: per-checkout mutation verdict cache. Content-keyed and local by
# design — a verdict depends on the interpreter and toolchain, which the key
# does not cover, so one from another machine imports an unchecked assumption.
.mutation-cache.json
